INT. GLASS GREENHOUSE - WEDDING REHEARSAL - EVENING

Ranks of potted orchids. Warm fog on the panes. A white aisle runner laid between fern beds. Folding chairs. A trellis arch drapes with unlit fairy lights.

ROSEMARY, 30s, the bride, in jeans and a linen blouse, stands at the arch. DEVLIN, 30s, the groom, in a rumpled suit, stands beside her. ANTOINETTE, 60s, the officiant, in a shawl, holds an index card. KIERAN, 30s, the best man, slouches against a pot of cymbidiums. SEUN, 20s, the maid of honor, in a floral wrap dress, holds a bouquet of paper flowers. LAVINIA, 50s, Rosemary's mother, perches on a chair with a clipboard.

LAVINIA
(to the group)
All right, everyone. Positions!

KIERAN
(to Seun)
Where do I stand?

SEUN
Next to the groom.

KIERAN
Which one's the groom?

DEVLIN
I'm the groom.

KIERAN
Oh. Yeah.

ANTOINETTE
(reading)
Dearly beloved.

ROSEMARY
Do we say that?

ANTOINETTE
It's traditional.

ROSEMARY
It's a little dead.

ANTOINETTE
It's very old.

LAVINIA
(to herself)
They'll be late for the caterer.

Seun glances at Kieran. Kieran glances at Seun. Both look away. She straightens the bouquet. He picks at a leaf. The fairy lights flick on, then off.

DEVLIN
(to Rosemary)
You look nervous.

ROSEMARY
I'm not.

DEVLIN
You're holding your breath.

ROSEMARY
It's the humidity.

DEVLIN
Ro.

ROSEMARY
He looked at her.

DEVLIN
Who?

ROSEMARY
(low)
Kieran. At Seun.

DEVLIN
They're the best man and the maid of honor. They're supposed to look at each other.

ROSEMARY
Not like that.

Antoinette clears her throat and taps the card.

ANTOINETTE
Does anyone object?

A silence. Everyone looks at one another.

LAVINIA
(to the group)
It's a rehearsal. No one objects.

KIERAN
Actually.

All heads turn. Kieran is looking at Seun. She stares back, wide-eyed.

KIERAN (CONT'D)
(to himself)
Nope. Never mind.

SEUN
(to herself)
Oh no.

The fairy lights blaze on, all at once, and a hundred small gold stars shine above the arch.
